+# Check that a variable living in an ARM D-register pair does not abort CodeView
+# emission.  D-register pairs such as D1_D2 are RegisterTuples: the odd-even
+# pairs deliberately have no Q register covering them (see TuplesOE2D in
+# ARMRegisterInfo.td), and the CodeView format has no register number for a
+# D-pair at all -- it encodes only S0-S31, D0-D31 and Q0-Q15.  There is
+# therefore no correct value to emit for such a register, so the variable's
+# location is dropped and the variable reports as optimized out.  Emitting a
+# wrong register, or one half of the pair, would be worse than emitting nothing.
+#
+# Before this was handled, getCodeViewRegNum() reached a report_fatal_error and
+# the whole object file was lost: "error in backend: unknown codeview register
+# D1_D2".  See https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/64278.
+#
+# The two variables here differ in exactly one respect -- whether their register
+# is representable in CodeView -- so 'qreg' doubles as the control: it must keep
+# a real def range, proving the fallible lookup did not disturb mappable
+# registers.
